&lt;li&gt;Take team-level accountability for cross-platform (iOS and Android) strategy, and for individual mobile delivery across the org&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee direction for software quality in partnership with QA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start shaping architecture governance and the architectural review process, including how staff/principal technical leverage is applied across teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own hiring pipeline direction, including interviewing and hiring decisions for open mobile roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a mobile capacity view into roadmap planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin to set direction for AI adoption and tooling efficiency across the mobile org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong working relationships and operating rhythms with Product and Design partners across the pillars, and build a product engineering culture across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;After 6 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead architecture governance and the ADR process end to end, including calling the bets that affect roadmap or resourcing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set Mobile Health direction and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the approach to AI adoption and tooling efficiency across the mobile org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own staff development and feedback across the mobile org, including promotion decisions and escalations, and actively develop current and future engineering leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion recognition and culture for the mobile team, and build project management / product-engineering capability across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As capacity allows, pick up select mobile IC work off the critical path to stay current&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a robust cross-functional operating model for Mobile: how the organization plans, prioritizes, and coordinates with Product, Design, Analytics, and other key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
